          {
            "id": "blk_about_bio_en",
            "type": "rich_text",
            "heading": "01 // Executive Biography",
            "paragraphs": [
              "Welcome to my digital workspace. I am an Electrical, Computer & Energy Engineering (ECE) Ph.D. student at the **University of Colorado Boulder**, specializing in **data-driven safety-critical control** and **statistical system identification**. My doctoral research centers on synthesizing Control Barrier Functions (CBFs) and optimization-based controller safety filters directly from trajectory data to provide formal safety guarantees for uncertain dynamical systems."
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "blk_about_pillars_en",
            "type": "bento_grid",
            "heading": "02 // Technical Expertise & Focus",
            "columns": 2,
            "items": [
              {
                "indexLabel": "MODULE 01 // SYSTEM ID",
                "title": "Statistical System Identification",
                "description": "Formulating mathematical state-space models and uncertainty bounds directly from input-output trajectory data."
              },
              {
                "indexLabel": "MODULE 02 // SAFETY CONTROL",
                "title": "Safety Filters - CBF & CG",
                "description": "Synthesizing data-driven Command Governor (CG) and Control Barrier Functions (CBFs) that enforce formal invariants."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "blk_about_tracks_en",
            "type": "cards_grid",
            "heading": "03 // Featured Tracks",
            "columns": 2,
            "items": [
              {
                "badge": "ECE PHD",
                "badgeStyle": "solid",
                "title": "Data-Driven Safety & System ID",
                "subtitle": "Safety-Critical Control & Safety Filters",
                "description": "Developing data-driven Control Barrier Functions (CBFs) and safety filtering frameworks to enforce formal safety guarantees for unmodeled linear systems.",
                "tags": [],
                "buttonLabel": "EXPLORE RESEARCH →",
                "actionType": "page",
                "target": "research"
              },
              {
                "badge": "CONTROL SYSTEMS",
                "badgeStyle": "outline",
                "title": "Controller Synthesis & Simulation",
                "subtitle": "Optimal Feedback & Simscape Modeling",
                "description": "Formulating optimization-based safety filters and robust closed-loop feedback controllers validated across multi-domain physical simulations in MATLAB Simulink.",
                "tags": [],
                "buttonLabel": "VIEW PROJECTS →",
                "actionType": "page",
